\description{
Five loaders for the five tables of the
\code{nba_stats_draft_combine} release, one file per table per season:
\code{load_nba_stats_draft_combine_stats()} (\code{draftcombinestats}, the
one-row-per-prospect summary of every measurement),
\code{load_nba_stats_draft_combine_anthro()} (\code{draftcombineplayeranthro},
body measurements), \code{load_nba_stats_draft_combine_drills()}
(\code{draftcombinedrillresults}, vertical leaps, agility and sprint),
\code{load_nba_stats_draft_combine_spot_shooting()}
(\code{draftcombinespotshooting}, made/attempted from five floor spots at 15
feet, the college three and the NBA three) and
\code{load_nba_stats_draft_combine_nonstationary_shooting()}
(\code{draftcombinenonstationaryshooting}, off-the-dribble and on-the-move
shooting).

The combine is held in May before the draft, so the season's START year
is the combine year: \code{seasons = 2024} reads the 2024 combine (the
\code{..._2025} asset). Columns a year's combine did not measure are all \code{NA}.
}
\examples{
\donttest{
  try(load_nba_stats_draft_combine_stats(seasons = most_recent_nba_stats_season()))
}
}
\seealso{
The publishing pipeline,
\url{https://github.com/sportsdataverse/hoopR-nba-stats-data}, the draft
results in \code{\link[=load_nba_stats_draft]{load_nba_stats_draft()}}, and the Python twins
\verb{sportsdataverse.nba.load_nba_stats_draft_combine_*()}.

